6. REAL AI-POWERED PRODUCT IMPORT BY URL

This is one of the most important features of Dokandari.

The admin dashboard must provide a dedicated feature named:

AI Bulk Product Import

The administrator should be able to provide one or multiple product URLs.

The system must attempt to import the product information, original product images, and original product videos from each supported source.

This must be a real import workflow, not a demo interface.

6.1 URL Input Interface

Provide:

- A single product URL input.
- A multiline URL input for multiple products.
- A CSV file upload option for product URLs.
- An Import Products button.
- A Validate URLs button.
- An import preview.
- Import progress.
- Import history.
- Error reporting.

The administrator must be able to paste product URLs directly into the import interface.

6.2 Supported Source Configuration

Build the import system using a configurable source-adapter architecture.

Use official APIs or authorized integration methods when available.

Support publicly accessible product pages where automated access is permitted.

For sources requiring authentication, special permissions, or platform-specific APIs, clearly identify the required authorization.

Do not claim universal compatibility with every website.

Some websites block automated access or restrict the downloading and reuse of their content. When a source cannot be accessed legally or technically, show a clear error and provide an appropriate alternative.

Do not bypass CAPTCHAs, authentication controls, anti-bot protections, or access restrictions.

6.3 Product Information Extraction

For every successfully processed URL, extract the available information:

- Product title.
- Product description.
- Product price.
- Original price, when available.
- Product category.
- Product SKU, when available.
- Brand, when available.
- Product variants.
- Available colors.
- Available sizes.
- Product specifications.
- Stock information, when accessible.
- Product image URLs.
- Product video URLs.
- Source product URL.

Extract original product information from the source whenever possible.

If the source provides structured product data, use it where appropriate.

If structured data is unavailable, use a permitted HTML extraction method or a connected AI vision/language service to analyze accessible content.

Do not invent unavailable product specifications, dimensions, materials, prices, or stock information.

If information cannot be verified, mark it as unavailable or requiring manual review.

6.4 Original Product Image Import

The importer must:

1. Identify the original product images available from the source.
2. Retrieve the images when access and reuse are permitted.
3. Upload imported image files to the configured product storage.
4. Save the resulting permanent storage references.
5. Associate the images with the correct product record.
6. Display image previews before publishing.
7. Allow the administrator to remove, reorder, or replace images.

Do not store temporary browser URLs as permanent product image references.

Do not report that an image has been imported unless the image was successfully retrieved and stored, or a clearly identified external reference was intentionally saved.

If the source blocks image retrieval, display an error and allow manual image upload.

Preserve the original downloaded image when possible.

Do not silently substitute unrelated images or AI-generated images for the source's original product images.

6.5 Original Product Video Import

Attempt to identify and import the source's original product videos where supported and authorized.

The system must:

- Identify accessible product video URLs.
- Retrieve video files when permitted.
- Upload retrieved video files to configured storage.
- Associate videos with the correct product.
- Generate playable video previews.
- Allow administrators to remove or reorder videos.
- Display accurate import status.

If a video cannot be downloaded, show the actual reason when known.

If external video embedding is permitted but downloading is not, offer a clearly labeled external video option.

Never show a fake video preview or claim a video has been downloaded when it has not.

6.6 AI-Assisted Data Processing

After extracting the available source information, use the configured AI service to help:

- Clean product titles.
- Generate improved product descriptions.
- Translate descriptions between English and Bengali when required.
- Suggest product categories.
- Identify visible colors.
- Generate SEO titles.
- Generate meta descriptions.
- Create image alt text.
- Organize product specifications.

Maintain the original source data separately from AI-generated content.

Allow administrators to switch between the original source description and the AI-improved description.

AI must not silently replace original product information.

6.7 Import Preview and Approval

Before publishing, show an editable preview containing:

- Product title.
- Description.
- Price.
- Category.
- Images.
- Videos.
- Variants.
- SKU.
- Source URL.
- Import warnings.
- Missing information.

Provide the following actions:

- Edit Product.
- Save as Draft.
- Import Product.
- Publish Product.
- Cancel Import.

The administrator must be able to edit the imported information before publication.

Do not publish products automatically unless an administrator has explicitly enabled an appropriate automatic publishing policy.

6.8 Multiple Product Import

When multiple URLs are provided, process them using a reliable background job or batch-processing system where appropriate.

For every product, record:

- Source URL.
- Import job ID.
- Processing status.
- Start time.
- Completion time.
- Product ID, if created.
- Success or failure.
- Error details.

Show accurate counts for:

- Total URLs submitted.
- Successfully imported products.
- Failed imports.
- Products requiring review.
- Products awaiting processing.

Allow failed imports to be retried.

Prevent duplicate imports using configurable matching rules, such as source URL, SKU, or an appropriate product fingerprint.

Do not report success until the corresponding operation has actually succeeded.

